# Castlevania: Curse of Darkness (4B4E002D), single route. lane.titleroutes
# session 48, 2026-10-01, from the generic `--route survey` soak
# 0-0-s-1790839398-titleroutes-2238193 (Thor, heat-stopped at 284/300s).
#
# Every earlier guess route for this title (castlevania-cod.first-run, two
# re-marks) never got past a menu: New Game landed on Name Entry, then on
# "Create new save data? Yes/No". The generic survey's 14 START/A cycles
# (not the guess route's handful) cleared whatever that save-data prompt
# and name entry needed, and its `mark play` frame (011651-play.png) and
# the one after it (011717-play.png) are confirmed by eye: a character
# standing in a gothic courtyard facing a gargoyle, then walking through
# the courtyard toward a gate -- real control, not a menu.
#
# So: 14 cycles, then the survey's own post-mark combat/move loop (A to
# attack/confirm, RX to turn the camera, LY to walk). DRAFT until a soak
# replays this file by name and the mark frame is reviewed again: the
# survey proved 14 cycles is ENOUGH, not that it is the fewest that work.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
mark booted
repeat 14 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
axis LY min
press A
wait 3
press A
wait 3
press A
wait 3
axis RX max
wait 0.5
axis RX mid
axis LY mid
wait 1
shot running
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    press A
    wait 3
    press A
    wait 3
    press A
    wait 3
    axis RX max
    wait 0.5
    axis RX mid
    axis LY mid
    wait 1
    shot play
}
